IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`
IMPORT `euca-s203-period`
IMPORT `euca-s202-work-test`
IMPORT `euca-s202-conditions`
IMPORT `euca-s202-account`

-- Section 202(a) with (b) and (c), put together: for one week, must extended compensation be
-- paid? Layer 1: the law, objectively. No new rule is stated here; each conjunct is a rule
-- from the module named beside it, and the whole is the conjunction the Act makes by saying that
-- "a State law shall provide" payment for the weeks and the people it describes (s 202(a)(1)) and
-- that paragraphs (3), (4), (5) and subsection (c) take the payment away.
-- "Payable" here means what the State law must provide under this title; a State law may
-- provide more (fork register). The relation: the individual's claim against the State, and the
-- State's duty to pay, which sections 202(a)(3) to (5) and 202(c) cut off, week by week.
-- One reading to know about (fork F-19): where the State law has chosen no method of measuring
-- employment under section 202(a)(5), this rule says "not payable", because it asks for the
-- result `the individual has the required employment`. The Act itself decides nothing in that
-- case; the not-covered value is kept by `the result of the employment requirement`, which
-- callers can ask directly (the seat question on employment does).

§ `Section 202: whether extended compensation is payable for a week`

§§ `The rules of paragraphs (3) and (4), unless paragraph (7) suspends them`

-- src:55 | “(7) Paragraphs (3) and (4) shall not apply to weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993, and before January 1, 1995, and no provision of State law in conformity with such paragraphs shall apply during such period.
@ref s 202(a)(3), (7) (src:55)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
      search IS A `Search for work`
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the work test bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` week offers search failure MEANS
        `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` week
    AND `the work test bars extended compensation for the week` week offers search failure

-- src:55 | “(7) Paragraphs (3) and (4) shall not apply to weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993, and before January 1, 1995, and no provision of State law in conformity with such paragraphs shall apply during such period.
@ref s 202(a)(4), (7) (src:55)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      disqualifications IS A LIST OF Disqualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a disqualification bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` week disqualifications MEANS
        `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` week
    AND `a disqualification still bars extended compensation` disqualifications

§§ `The week as a whole`

-- src:26 | a State law shall provide the payment of extended compensation shall be made, for any week of unemployment which begins in the individual’s eligibility period
-- src:53 | an individual shall not be eligible for extended compensation unless
@ref s 202(a)(1), (3), (4), (5), (7) and s 202(b), (c) (src:26 src:53)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      benefitYear IS A `Benefit year`
      period IS AN `Extended benefit period`
      position IS A `Regular compensation position`
      offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
      search IS A `Search for work`
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
      disqualifications IS A LIST OF Disqualification
      employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
      interstate IS AN `Interstate claim`
      account IS AN `Account facts`
      `extended compensation already paid to the individual in the benefit year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`extended compensation is payable for the week` week benefitYear period position offers search failure disqualifications employment interstate account `extended compensation already paid to the individual in the benefit year` MEANS
        `the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` week benefitYear position (`the week is in the individual's eligibility period` week benefitYear period)
    AND (NOT `the work test bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` week offers search failure)
    AND (NOT `a disqualification bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` week disqualifications)
    AND `the result of the employment requirement` employment EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
    AND (NOT `payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` interstate)
    AND `extended compensation already paid to the individual in the benefit year` LESS THAN (`the amount the extended compensation account must hold` account)

-- src:54 | “(6) No payment shall be made under this Act [see Short Title of 1970 Amendment note set out under section 3311 of this title] to any State in respect of any extended compensation or sharable regular compensation paid to any individual for any week if, under the rules of paragraphs (3), (4), and (5), extended compensation would not have been payable to such individual for such week.
@ref s 202(a)(6) (src:54)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
      search IS A `Search for work`
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
      disqualifications IS A LIST OF Disqualification
      employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the State may not be paid its share of extended compensation paid for the week` week offers search failure disqualifications employment MEANS
    `no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` week
        (`the work test bars extended compensation for the week` week offers search failure)
        (`a disqualification still bars extended compensation` disqualifications)
        (`the result of the employment requirement` employment)
